&lt;h4&gt;About the role&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kubernetes optimization is Cast AI&#39;s core platform and &lt;strong&gt;our main competitive battleground&lt;/strong&gt;. As that surface keeps growing, across the Node Autoscaler, Karpenter Enterprise Suite, and the Workload Autoscaler, we need one person to own the full commercial story.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The core platform is growing fast&lt;/strong&gt;, faster than our commercial story has kept pace with. That&#39;s the opportunity: you&#39;ll build the unified narrative this portfolio is ready for, set the launch discipline that keeps it consistent as new features ship, and give sales messaging they can actually reuse instead of rebuilding it deal by deal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a highly technical and strategic role&lt;/strong&gt;. You&#39;ll act as the voice of the product in the market and the voice of the customer internally, which means translating the same product differently for platform engineers, DevOps and SRE leaders, FinOps teams, VPs of Engineering, and CTOs. That requires real fluency in how software runs, built through marketing technical products, not necessarily through an engineering background. We operate automation-first and market-obsessed, so you&#39;re expected to treat customer and market signals as the input behind every decision, and to build AI-assisted workflows that make this function faster and more consistent over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll report to the Director of Product Marketing, who sets priorities and goals with you, and you&#39;ll have real support from Product, Content, Demand Gen, Customer Success, and Design.&lt;/p&gt;
