&lt;li&gt;Launches land stronger, with measurable product adoption or pipeline impact tied to them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive win rates improve, and the field actually uses the competitive materials you build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sales has real confidence in the product narrative, not just access to a deck.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer proof points are quantified, not anecdotal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A repeatable customer and win/loss feedback loop exists and demonstrably shapes Product and GTM decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Requirements:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in product marketing, with real experience in cloud infrastructure, Kubernetes, DevOps, developer tools, FinOps, observability, databases, or a similarly technical B2B market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency. You can talk to engineers and technical audiences without sounding shallow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of turning complex technical products into clear, differentiated messaging for both practitioners and executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent writing, backed by work samples such as positioning, launch content, sales narratives, or technical thought leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading launches and influencing adoption, pipeline, or competitive outcomes, not just producing launch collateral.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading customer, market, or win/loss research that actually changed a product or go-to-market decision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional work with Product, Engineering, Sales, Customer Success, and Growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating without a mature playbook. This function is still being built, and you&#39;ll be defining a process as much as executing against one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English, written and spoken.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What would make you stand out:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
