&lt;p&gt;Over 2,100 companies already rely on Cast AI, including Akamai, BMW, Cisco, FICO, HuggingFace, NielsenIQ, Swisscom, and TGS.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global team, diverse perspectives&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We&#39;re headquartered in Miami, but our impact is international. We take a global and intentional approach to diversity. Today, Cast AI operates across 34 countries spanning Europe, North America, Latin America, and APAC, bringing a wide range of perspectives into how we build and lead.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unicorn momentum&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;In January 2026, we achieved unicorn status with a strategic investment from Pacific Alliance Ventures, the corporate venture arm of Shinsegae Group (a $50+ billion Korean conglomerate). Our valuation now exceeds $1 billion, and we&#39;re just getting started.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join us as we build the future of autonomous infrastructure.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;About the role&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cast AI is the leading Kubernetes cloud cost optimization platform, trusted by engineering and finance teams to dramatically reduce cloud spend. We&#39;re growing fast and looking for sharp, execution-oriented people to help scale our go-to-market motion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a GTM Enablement Manager, you will design and deliver programs that sharpen the skills, knowledge, and behaviors of our revenue teams — from new hire onboarding to ongoing product training and sales methodology coaching. You will work closely with Sales, Business Development, Marketing, Product, and Customer Success to ensure every customer-facing employee is equipped to have high-quality conversations, convert pipeline, and deliver exceptional customer experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Requirements:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in sales enablement, GTM enablement, or a related learning and development role within a B2B SaaS company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success designing and delivering enablement programs that measurably improved rep ramp time or sales performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the B2B SaaS enterprise sales cycle, including MEDDPICC or similar enterprise sales methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with Product Marketing to create sales-ready content and competitive positioning materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent facilitation and presentation skills; comfortable leading large group training sessions as well as 1:1 coaching conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven mindset — you measure what you build and iterate based on outcomes, not just feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management skills; able to manage multiple workstreams and deadlines independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with enablement and sales tools such as Salesforce, Gong, Hubspot, Outreach, or similar platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written communication skills with the ability to distill complex technical topics into clear, compelling narratives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience enabling sales teams in the cloud infrastructure, Kubernetes, FinOps, or DevOps space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with cloud cost management concepts, Kubernetes architecture, or related technical domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building enablement programs for global teams across AMER, LATAM, EMEA, and APAC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to Sales Engineering or Solutions Engineering enablement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Responsibilities&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and manage a comprehensive onboarding program for new AEs, BDRs, SEs, and Customer Success hires that accelerates time-to-productivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain a structured, scalable sales training curriculum covering CAST AI&#39;s product, competitive positioning, sales methodology, and buyer personas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Marketing to translate new product releases and messaging updates into field-ready training content, battlecards, and talk tracks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and facilitate live training sessions, workshops, role-plays, and certifications — in-person and virtual — across global teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and organize the enablement content library (playbooks, decks, one-pagers, objection handling guides) ensuring materials are current and easily accessible – experience with RevSpace or similar enablement platforms a plus)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure the impact of enablement programs through completion rates, assessment scores, ramp time, and downstream sales performance metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify skill gaps and knowledge deficiencies through analysis of rep performance data, call reviews (Gong), and manager feedback; develop targeted interventions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Systems on tool adoption training to ensure reps are effectively using Salesforce, Outreach, and other platforms in their daily workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and manage an ongoing coaching cadence in partnership with front-line sales managers to reinforce skills learned in formal training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the GTM enablement calendar, coordinating delivery across all functions and geographies to minimize disruption to selling time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales Leadership and RevOps to roll out pipeline generation sales plays to the field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive adoption of AI-powered tools and workflows to improve seller productivity, coaching effectiveness, prospecting, content creation, and overall GTM execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
